  "base_commit": "b5f8518379b77c3b62a7a9d2b52f6c76cda09bd5",
  "pr_number": 15154,
  "issue_number": 15153,
  "issue_title": "Custom elements: async components nested \u22653 levels crash with `TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'provides')` \u2014 chained child resolve races its parent's mount",
  "issue_body": "### Vue version\n\n3.5.40 (`latest` at the time of writing \u2014 the inline repro pins it; also reproduced on 3.5.13, 3.5.17, 3.5.30 and 3.6.0-rc.2; 3.4.38 \u2014 before the nested-async chaining existed \u2014 crashes with the same null dereference in the older `_setParent` provides copy inside `vnode.ce`)\n\n### Link to minimal reproduction\n\nhttps://play.vuejs.org/#\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open the reproduction link and watch the console: `mounted x-inner` never appears \u2014 the element crashes with an unhandled `TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'provides')` and never mounts. (The playground variant inserts the nested markup dynamically after the `define()` calls; dynamic and parser-created markup crash identically.)\n2. Parser-created (static server-HTML-style) variant \u2014 self-contained single file, no build step (save as `repro.html`, serve statically, open in any browser; Chromium, Firefox and WebKit all reproduce):\n\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n<title>nested async custom elements repro</title>\n<x-outer>\n  <x-middle>\n    <div>\n      <x-inner>inner light dom</x-inner>\n    </div>\n  </x-middle>\n</x-outer>\n<script type=\"module\">\n  import {\n    defineCustomElement,\n    defineAsyncComponent,\n    h,\n  } from \"https://unpkg.com/vue@3.5.40/dist/vue.esm-browser.js\";\n\n  // Delays chosen so the middle level settles AFTER its child: outer fast,\n  // middle slow, inner fast. This crashes on 100% of loads.\n  const delays = { \"x-outer\": 50, \"x-middle\": 300, \"x-inner\": 10 };\n\n  const makeComponent = (name) => ({\n    name,\n    mounted() {\n      console.log(`mounted ${name}`);\n    },\n    render() {\n      return h(\"div\", { style: \"display:block;padding:6px;border:1px solid #888\" }, [name, h(\"slot\")]);\n    },\n  });\n\n  const makeLoader = (tag) => () =>\n    new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(() => resolve(makeComponent(tag)), delays[tag]));\n\n  // Define the three tags parent-first.\n  for (const tag of [\"x-outer\", \"x-middle\", \"x-inner\"]) {\n    customElements.define(tag, defineCustomElement(defineAsyncComponent(makeLoader(tag))));\n  }\n\n  window.addEventListener(\"error\", (e) => console.error(\"UNCAUGHT:\", e.message));\n  window.addEventListener(\"unhandledrejection\", (e) =>\n    console.error(\"UNHANDLED REJECTION:\", e.reason?.message ?? e.reason),\n  );\n</script>\n```\n\n### What is expected?\n\nAll three elements mount ancestor-first: `mounted x-outer`, `mounted x-middle`, `mounted x-inner`. The nested-async chaining added in 3.5.0 (37ccb9b, \"delay mounting of custom elements with async parent\", closing #9341 / #8127 / #9351) exists to guarantee exactly this.\n\n### What is actually happening?\n\n```\nmounted x-outer\nUNHANDLED REJECTION: Cannot read properties of null (reading 'provides')\nmounted x-middle\n```\n\n`x-inner` crashes in `VueElement._mount \u2192 _inheritParentContext` (`runtime-dom` \u2014 `parent._instance.provides` is dereferenced guarded only by `parent && this._app`), never mounts, and is left permanently half-resolved: `_resolved: true`, `_instance: null`, shadow root empty. Nothing ever retries it, no error surfaces through `app.config.errorHandler`, and any `provide`/`inject` inheritance it should have received is lost. Its own descendants (at deeper nesting) then crash against it in cascade.\n\n### Any additional comments?\n\n**Analysis** (why depth \u2265 3 is the trigger)\n\n`connectedCallback` of a child under a *pending* async parent chains:\n\n```js\nthis._pendingResolve = parent._pendingResolve.then(() => {\n  this._pendingResolve = undefined;\n  this._resolveDef();\n});\n```\n\n- For an **unchained** parent (depth 2), `parent._pendingResolve` is the parent's own `_resolveDef()` flow, which settles after the parent has mounted \u2192 2-level nesting is safe. The variants table below confirms: 2 levels never crash.\n- For a **chained** parent (depth \u2265 3), `parent._pendingResolve` is itself a chain promise \u2014 and that promise settles when the parent's `_resolveDef()` **returns** (i.e. when the parent's async load *starts*), not when the parent mounts.\n\nSo once the first unchained ancestor mounts, the whole chain unwinds within a few microtasks: every deeper level's loader fires nearly simultaneously and mount order degenerates to **network settlement order**. Any child whose async definition settles before its parent has mounted hits `_inheritParentContext` while `parent._instance === null` and throws. With real-network chunk timings the victim set varies per load, so in an app this presents as a flaky, page-dependent breakage; with the fixed delays above it is 100% deterministic.\n\nVariants checked (each re-run in a real browser):\n\n| Variant | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| 3 levels, middle slowest | crashes every load |\n| 3 levels, inner slowest | clean (race direction confirmed) |\n| 2 levels | clean (chained parent required) |\n| plain `<div>` between levels | still crashes (structure-independent) |\n| markup inserted dynamically after all `define()` calls | still crashes |\n| all loaders instant | clean (microtask FIFO protects when nothing is pending) |\n\n`_inheritParentContext` (#13219, ~3.5.14) did not introduce the race \u2014 it converted a pre-existing silent misordering into a hard crash. 3.4.38 (no chaining) and 3.5.13 (chaining, pre-#13219) fail with the same null dereference in the older `_setParent` provides-copy path.\n\n**Suggested direction** \u2014 either (or both):\n\n1. Chain the child to the parent's actual **mount**, not to `_resolveDef()` returning \u2014 e.g. resolve the parent's `_pendingResolve` only after `_mount()` has run, so the guarantee the chaining was built for (\"ancestor mounts before descendant\") holds at any depth.\n2. Guard `_inheritParentContext` against `parent._instance === null` and defer context inheritance until the parent instance exists, instead of throwing away the child permanently on an unhandled rejection.\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-08-04T07:40:44Z",
